+## firing it out of the store
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired out of whatever the
+magazine holds, and those are never the same list. Give any show command the
+magazine book and the compile draws from it:
+
+```
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig \
+  --magazine magazine.csv --pull vn2405,vn2413
+```
+
+Every cue is issued a lot, oldest lot first. A cue whose shell has run out is
+given the nearest thing the store holds, same calibre before same handling band,
+and it keeps its own cue time while lifting on the stand in's flight. `--pull`
+sets lots aside first, which is what a recall or a wet case means. A cue nothing
+can cover is an error rather than a firing table for a shell nobody owns, and the
+cue sheet grows a lot column so the crew can trace what left the building.
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
 ## the commands
